    "title": "Tony Khan - 'Developing Steven Borden Is A Huge Priority For AEW' - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n14 minutes ago\nTony Khan has confirmed that AEW is currently focused on developing Steven Borden, the son of WWE Hall of Famer Sting.\nThe AEW President spoke about Borden’s progress during a recent appearance on the “Battleground” podcast. Although Borden has appeared for AEW in limited roles, including dark matches, he has not yet made his official television debut as a signed performer.\nREAD MORE: Celeste Bonin Loved Wrestling, But Has No Desire To Go Back\nREAD MORE: Ex-WWE Star Accused Of ‘Buying Views’ For His YouTube Channel\nKhan spoke highly of Borden’s potential, noting that AEW sees him as a long-term project. He said,\n“Steven still has never been on AEW TV, but he’s somebody we’re developing. I have so much respect for Steven. He’s a rising young wrestler. He played college football at Kentucky. I followed his football career, and now I’m proud to say we’re working on developing him as a pro wrestler for AEW.”\nHe continued, “Developing him for the future is a huge priority to me and everyone in AEW.”\nNOTE: If you have any news tips or podcast recaps that you’d like to send in for us to post (full credit will be given to you), please email me at RClarkPWS@Yahoo.com .",
    "summary": "Tony Khan has confirmed that AEW is currently focused on developing Steven Borden, the son of WWE Hall of Famer Sting. The AEW President spoke about Borden’s progress during a recent appearance on the “Battleground” podcast. Although Borden has appeared for AEW in limited roles, including dark matches, he has not yet made his official television debut as a signed performer.",
